{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions","id":900957,"title":"Extended Actions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-27T07:43:36-07:00","id":900957,"title":"Extended Actions","content":"The rules text for extended actions don't say anything (unless I missed it) about whether you can continue rolling after you have reached the requisite number of successes. Does anyone know what the intent of the developers is here? Alternatively, what's your ruling on this in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:03:09-07:00","id":900973,"title":"","content":"You don't continue chiseling away after the bust is done. You don't keep trying to fix an engine after it begins to purr anew like when it was new. No, you don't keep rolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:05:14-07:00","id":900976,"title":"","content":"That's also my preferred interpretation, but do you have any reason to think that's what was intended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:31:46-07:00","id":901002,"title":"","content":"Common sense, extrapolation from 1e, etc, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:42:58-07:00","id":901018,"title":"","content":"Most have the result trigger upon completion, with successes over the target meaning nothing. I guess, you might try to keep rolling to get an Exceptional Success, but just raw numbers won't do it. So it is already kind of pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T19:09:22-07:00","id":901639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=901018#post901018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most have the result trigger upon completion, with successes over the target meaning nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I think it should work, but do you have a reference to back up this interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T19:18:11-07:00","id":901646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=901002#post901002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...extrapolation from 1e...</div> </div> </div> </div>I took a quick glance through the 1E core book, and I couldn't find this rule. Do you have a reference?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T09:03:06-07:00","id":902084,"title":"","content":"The fact that you can't find anything in the rules talking about continuing to roll after successfully completing an extended action is itself a citation that it can't be done. If it could, the rules would need to say so. The rules tell you what you <i>can</i> do, not what you <i>can't</i> do.<br /> <br /> Besides, what would even be the point of continuing to roll after succeeding? All the exceptional success results do on extended actions is make it easier to reach the target number of successes faster, either by cutting down time interval per roll or reducing the target number. Once you've reached that target number, pushing for an exceptional success won't make any difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T16:37:04-07:00","id":902360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=902084#post902084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, what would even be the point of continuing to roll after succeeding? All the exceptional success results do on extended actions is make it easier to reach the target number of successes faster, either by cutting down time interval per roll or reducing the target number. Once you've reached that target number, pushing for an exceptional success won't make any difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically this is not true, as you can also use an exceptional succes on one of the rolls to get the exceptional success result for the action. So if you want that result, being able to keep rolling could be useful, as it could be faster than starting a new extended action for the same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:16:21-07:00","id":902440,"title":"","content":"As Penta says, if you want the exceptional success benefit, there is reason to keep rolling.<br /> <br /> Narratively, suppose I'm writing a computer program. Achieving the required number of successes gets me a program that functions as desired. I could, however, keep working on the program to optimize it. This risks ruining the whole thing (a dramatic failure), but it certainly makes sense that I can keep rolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T19:47:14-07:00","id":902454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=902440#post902440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Penta says, if you want the exceptional success benefit, there is reason to keep rolling.<br /> <br /> Narratively, suppose I'm writing a computer program. Achieving the required number of successes gets me a program that functions as desired. I could, however, keep working on the program to optimize it. This risks ruining the whole thing (a dramatic failure), but it certainly makes sense that I can keep rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like you already know how you want to run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-29-2016, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T20:55:18-07:00","id":902468,"title":"","content":"I'll add a citation from the book:<br /> <br /> &quot;...apply the exceptional success result of the action when you complete your goal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Read literally, you can't apply the exceptional success result if your goal is already completed. The ability to apply an exceptional success to the final results only applies if you haven't hit your goal yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T21:02:17-07:00","id":902470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=902468#post902468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll add a citation from the book:<br /> <br /> &quot;...apply the exceptional success result of the action when you complete your goal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Read literally, you can't apply the exceptional success result if your goal is already completed. The ability to apply an exceptional success to the final results only applies if you haven't hit your goal yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the best evidence yet of the dev's intention, though it is a little bit nitpicky. Thanks for the citation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T21:04:12-07:00","id":902471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=902454#post902454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...slewed...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with this term, so I can't be sure what you mean, but in my second post, I stated that I prefer to rule that you cannot continue rolling. This is an ongoing discussion in my group, and the programming example came up to counter the &quot;it doesn't make narrative sense to continue rolling&quot; argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:53:01-07:00","id":902598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=902471#post902471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar with this term, so I can't be sure what you mean, but in my second post, I stated that I prefer to rule that you cannot continue rolling. This is an ongoing discussion in my group, and the programming example came up to counter the &quot;it doesn't make narrative sense to continue rolling&quot; argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally the Exceptional Success result means that your character got a better outcome than expected. But I don't think its against the rules to let a character shift the goalposts and try to achieve more than originally intended, thereby increasing the number of successes needed to complete the extended action. Although this might be better modelled by starting a new Extended roll, to for example optimize the computer program you talked about.<br /> <br /> Another option is to have different levels of success linked to different amounts of successes in Extended Actions. This has been recommended in the past for Extended Actions to uncover information, but there is no reason it could not work for other actions. When researching, you would get new information every few successes, and the action would not really &quot;fail&quot; if you didn't reach the goal. Getting less than the full amount of successes would just mean getting incomplete information. You could also use this rules for other actions, for example requiring 10 successes for a barely functional computer program (that perhaps gives a penalty), 20 successes for the baseline one, and 30 successes for the optimized one including extra functions. An exceptional success could then give you the computer program one level higher than the level achieved, without getting all the necessary successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T04:29:44-07:00","id":902618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=902440#post902440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Penta says, if you want the exceptional success benefit, there is reason to keep rolling.<br /> <br /> Narratively, suppose I'm writing a computer program. Achieving the required number of successes gets me a program that functions as desired. I could, however, keep working on the program to optimize it. This risks ruining the whole thing (a dramatic failure), but it certainly makes sense that I can keep rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div> This makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T04:32:36-07:00","id":902621,"title":"","content":"Perfectionist Merut: Add 5 successes needed to suceed on an extended action, in exchange its concidered an automatic exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Just an idea for a merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:20:03-07:00","id":902658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/900957-extended-actions?p=902621#post902621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfectionist Merut: Add 5 successes needed to suceed on an extended action, in exchange its concidered an automatic exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Just an idea for a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>An alternate version: You achieve an exceptional success on any extended action with 3 successes in any single roll, instead of five. Drawback: All extended actions, even those where you are unable to benefit from this effect, require 3 additional successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-29-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}